la xorxes. cusku di'e



{zi'e} should not really be necessary. I don't think any
ambiguity could arise from making it optional, but it would
still be useful because it makes many terminators elidable.

'zi'e' always terminates only the noi-phrase immediately in front of it, 
and so as far as I can tell, it's exactly equivalent to 'ku'o', and 
could always be replaced by it, if an arbitrary number of noi-phrases 
were allowed in a row.



mu'o mi'e .adam.
